From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: World of Warcraft <warcraft@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 06:16:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] CascLib: the plain file calls on musl

musl has no stat64, lseek64, ftruncate64 or off64_t (since 1.2.4); its own are 64-bit. CascLib
mapped them for macOS only. Used by the map extractors, which read the client's CASC storage.
---
 dep/CascLib/src/CascPort.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dep/CascLib/src/CascPort.h b/dep/CascLib/src/CascPort.h
index 5d9a710..4d4a278 100644
--- a/dep/CascLib/src/CascPort.h
+++ b/dep/CascLib/src/CascPort.h
@@ -199,7 +199,8 @@
 #endif // !PLATFORM_WINDOWS
 
 // 64-bit calls are supplied by "normal" calls on Mac
-#if defined(PLATFORM_MAC)
+// musl (Linux without glibc) has no large-file names either: its stat and off_t are 64-bit.
+#if defined(PLATFORM_MAC) || (defined(PLATFORM_LINUX) && !defined(__GLIBC__))
   #define stat64  stat
   #define fstat64 fstat
   #define lseek64 lseek
